    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). AcceptanceBase is abstract and AuditLogCapture is a helper, so `AcceptanceTest` is the single runnable test class, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-match (\"possible duplicate\") rule for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a different telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after the existing hard-duplicate identity check, added `applyPossibleDuplicate(owner)`. The new method finds the lowest-id existing owner whose normalized last name and postcode match the new owner's but whose telephone differs; if found it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<matching id>`, otherwise `possibleDuplicate=false`. Last-name comparison reuses the existing `normalizeHouseholdField` (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) for consistency with the other rules.\n\n2. **`Owner` model** \u2014 added two persistent fields `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`, `possible_duplicate`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`, `possible_duplicate_of`) with getters/setters, so the flags survive a later `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct maps them by name automatically.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the two new columns to the `owners` table, and appended the two `NULL` values to the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the only data file using positional inserts; the others use explicit column lists).\n\nI persisted the flags to the database rather than computing them transiently, since `GET` returns them as values fixed at creation, which requires them to outlive the create request in a real deployment.",
